. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * 
. 
.         * We consider a model using two-stage least squares
. 
.         * As a good proxy of gender equality in the household (hypothesis 3),
>  we use the share of housework performed by men (childcare + household chores
> ).
.         * The more gender-equal a household is, the more the man contributes 
> to housework.
.         * Accordingly, we run a regression analysis where we instrument "havi
> ng at least one daughter" with a dummy equal to one if the first born was a d
> augher,
.         * and we use "share_males" as dependent variable.
. 
. 
. ivregress 2sls share_males (d_daughter = daughterFB) sumkids age age2 agefb a
> gefb2 agepartner agepartner2 sumkids_mv age_mv age2_mv agefb_mv agefb2_mv age
> partner_mv agepartner2_mv i.syear, vce(cluster cid)
